One important change to your folder structure

Because you're using Next.js, I would slightly adjust the structure you originally wrote.

Instead of thinking:

app/
components/
features/
lib/
services/
schemas/
types/

as completely independent architecture, use them roughly like this:

Hardware-E-Shop/
│
├── app/
│   ├── api/
│   ├── (customer)/
│   └── (admin)/
│
├── components/
│   ├── ui/
│   └── shared/
│
├── features/
│   ├── products/
│   ├── cart/
│   ├── checkout/
│   ├── orders/
│   └── procurement/
│
├── lib/
│   ├── supabase/
│   ├── auth/
│   └── utils/
│
├── services/
│   ├── product.service.ts
│   ├── cart.service.ts
│   ├── order.service.ts
│   ├── payment.service.ts
│   └── procurement.service.ts
│
├── schemas/
│   ├── product.schema.ts
│   ├── cart.schema.ts
│   ├── order.schema.ts
│   └── payment.schema.ts
│
├── types/
│
├── supabase/
│   ├── migrations/
│   └── seed/
│
├── public/
│
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
└── README.md

But don't create all the actual files yet.

We're only establishing the architecture.